    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW26soxvhU7ZUKxFfmfYC5BAR)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main` (e8e60bee); independent of every other open PR in code.\n- Text conflict possible with #447: both add a part to `docs/tangles/vulpea/sp-vulpea.org` before `sp-vulpea-org-ql.el` and edit the intro table and load-order bullets. Keep both sides if it happens.\n- Touches `sp-vulpea-ext.el` (one `require`) and `sp-helper-funct.el` (a hook in `sp-copy-last-message`); #447 touches `sp-vulpea-ui.el`, so no conflict there.\n- Merged in any order nothing breaks.\n- After merging: restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`); nothing to retarget.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Request:** a small command to eval on a heading with an ID, to see whether it is backlinked anywhere in the vault; `embark-act` on the result opens a temporary buffer with the backlink locations.\n- **New module** `sp-vulpea-backlink-check` (`libraries/modules/vulpea/`), documented as a bullet-point part in `sp-vulpea.org`; required from `sp-vulpea-ext`.\n- `M-x sp-vulpea-backlink-check` (or eval `(sp-vulpea-backlink-check)`) on a heading with an `ID`:\n  - Echo area: `3 backlinks from 2 notes` or `not backlinked`.\n  - Heading without `ID` or non-Org buffer: a `user-error`.\n  - One `vulpea-db-query-links-to` call, no file reads, so it is fast. Headings with an ID are notes in Vulpea, so heading-level links are found. Self-links are not counted.\n- **Embark:** the result is a propertized string; target type `sp-vulpea-backlinks`, target = the heading ID.\n  - While the message is still in the echo area, `embark-act` acts on it directly (`current-message`); nothing is copied or added to the kill ring.\n  - Also offered for `sp-vulpea-backlink-check-timeout` seconds (default 10) after the check, or on the result line in `*Messages*`.\n  - `embark-act` then `RET` (or `s`): `*vulpea backlinks: TITLE*`, grouped by source note, each entry with its heading, line number and the line of context. `RET`/click jumps, `n`/`p` move, `g` refreshes, `q` quits. Open buffers are read instead of the file, so unsaved edits count.\n  - Embark is configured in `with-eval-after-load`, like `sp-litdb` and `sp-tab-psearch`.\n- **If the message is already gone:** `M-x sp-copy-last-message`, then `embark-act`.\n  - `sp-copy-last-message` has a new abnormal hook, `sp-copy-last-message-functions`; a function may return the copied text as a propertized string, which the `Copied: ...` message then shows. The kill ring still gets plain text.\n  - `sp-vulpea-backlink-check-restore` is on the hook and finds the text among the last 20 results (`sp-vulpea-backlink-check-history-size`). Same text from two headings: the newest wins.\n- Tests: `tests/sp-vulpea-backlink-check-test.el`, 21 ERT tests pass on Emacs 29.3 batch (counts, singular, none, self-links, command, no ID, target finder and timeout, restore, the copy hook, locations, buffer, `n`/`p`, visit, open buffer wins). Vulpea is stubbed, sources are real temp files. `.el` files and test are tangled from the docs; the existing grouped-backlinks tests still pass. `when-let*` only, no CHANGELOG edit.\n- **Not tested** with real Vulpea, Embark or the GUI: whether `:pos` of a heading-level source matches the file, whether the echo-area message is still there when `C-.` runs, and whether `*Messages*` keeps text properties (the restore path does not depend on it).\n\n## Manual testing\n\nMac, `~/.config/emacs-modular`, a note with a heading that has an `ID` and is linked from another note.\n\n- [ ] Check out: `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 450-backlink-check; git checkout 450-backlink-check`, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] Unit tests: `cd ~/.config/emacs-modular; emacs -Q --batch -l tests/sp-vulpea-backlink-check-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` → 21 pass\n- [ ] On a linked heading with an ID: `M-x sp-vulpea-backlink-check` shows `N backlinks from M notes`\n- [ ] Eval `(sp-vulpea-backlink-check)` with `C-x C-e` on the same heading: same message\n- [ ] `C-.` (`embark-act`) right after: the target is `sp-vulpea-backlinks`; `RET` opens `*vulpea backlinks: …*`; the kill ring is unchanged\n- [ ] In that buffer: each entry shows the source note, heading, line and context; `RET` jumps to the link, `n`/`p` move, `g` refreshes, `q` quits\n- [ ] A link from a heading (not the file top) is counted and shown (heading-level link)\n- [ ] A heading nobody links to: `not backlinked`; `embark-act` then `RET` shows \"Not backlinked.\"\n- [ ] A heading without an `ID`: error \"This heading has no ID\"\n- [ ] Let the message disappear (do something else for more than 10 seconds), then `M-x sp-copy-last-message`: it shows `Copied: …` and `C-.` offers the target\n- [ ] `sp-copy-last-message` on an ordinary message still copies it (`C-y` pastes it) and shows `Copied: …`\n- [ ] Open `*Messages*`, put point on the result line, `C-.`: the target is offered (only if `*Messages*` keeps the properties)\n- [ ] Time it on the real vault: the echo-area answer is instant\n- [ ] Regression: the grouped backlinks sidebar and the `vulpea-ui` widget still work\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`.\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`; restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- Fish shell works for all of the above; no yadm steps.\n\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAjRWkNrzYxSeHCHJC\n",
